#. Diagram label
msgid "approve"
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-component-edit-review.bpmn:110
#. Diagram label
msgid "Ask for review with staging deep links [staging-review]"
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-component-edit-review.bpmn:111
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Ask the person in the reviewing role, following staging-review's deep-link rule: one deep link per changed page and anchor on STAGING/<slug>/, each beside the same page on main as before (or \"new page\"), the pages taken from the change (rendered-impact) rather than chosen; no preview yet is said, not hidden. The request leads with what changed in prose, then the links, the before/after and the checker's findings, and puts its question in interaction-modality's form. Where it goes is a judgement, and more than one place may be right: this conversation, the GitHub issue the work came from, the pull request; each place carries the same links. A comment tagged on the PR becomes a review-comment todo (review-comments)."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-component-edit-review.bpmn:42
#. Diagram label
msgid "Authoring agent"
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-component-edit-review.bpmn:120
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "cat-harness's generic review, not a copy of it: classify what changed, review it, and record the decision as a qa-review/v1 QaReview whose subject is the component and whose Decision carries the reviewing role. The reviewer reads the staged page and the before/after; for a figure or table, the visual-diff picture and its changed-pixel count; for a form, the wireframe (wireframe-design-review; at L3 its Questionnaire follows fhir-questionnaire-wireframe). What to judge per component is the skill l2-component-edit-review's column \"the reviewer judges\"."
msgstr ""

