#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-component-edit-review.bpmn:74
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Create or change the component with the authoring skill the call names (l2-dak-authoring, bpmn-authoring, dmn-authoring or terminology-management), one component per pass. On rework, apply the review's findings; a fix the reviewer wrote in an AuditNote is applied as given. An adapted component is edited against its pinned upstream, so the before side of the diff is that upstream, not an empty file."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-component-edit-review.bpmn:43
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Does everything except judge. Edits the component with the authoring skill the call names, runs the component's checker, renders it and makes the before/after preview on a staged build, hands the component on without waiting, and asks for review with staging deep links. Prepares the review material and never records the verdict (smart-guideline-end-to-end, rule 4). On request-changes it edits again; on reject it reopens the stage upstream and flags what was derived from it."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-component-edit-review.bpmn:73
#. Diagram label
msgid "Edit the component [l2-component-edit-review]"
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-component-edit-review.bpmn:144
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "File a bean against the stage that chose the rejected source or dependency (check for an existing bean first), and mark every asset derived from this component adjudication: rejected-upstream on its wasDerivedFrom edge. Nothing is deleted ahead of time: the re-derivation may come out the same."
msgstr ""

