msgid "One L2 DAK component — agent edits, a person reviews"
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-component-edit-review.bpmn:28
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "One pass over one L2 DAK component: the agent edits it, runs its checker, renders and stages it with a before/after, and hands it on; review forks off beside that hand-on and never holds it up, because adjudication is QA, not a gate. That is the owner's ruling of 2026-10-14. Called by each authoring track of l2-dak-authoring.bpmn (Process_L2Dak), one call per component pass. The call's inputs, which are the only things that differ between components (skill l2-component-edit-review, \"The inputs, per component\"): - component: personas and user scenarios (C2, C3), business processes (C4), core data elements and glossary (C5) with their terminology bindings, decision-support and scheduling logic (C6, C7), indicators and requirements (C8, C9); - authoring skill: l2-dak-authoring, bpmn-authoring, dmn-authoring or terminology-management, named on the calling activity, so it joins this process's skills along the call path (review-task.bpmn's scoped composition); - renderer and diff: what the reviewer looks at, before and after; - checker: the mechanical checks the agent runs before asking anyone; - reviewing role: the person who takes on this process's reviewer lane for the call. One process rather than one per component because nothing but those inputs differs: DMN's test cases are its checker, BPMN's picture is its renderer, the glossary's term diff (dak-data-dictionary-diff.ts) is its diff and its binding check its checker, and traceability to L1 is the checker of personas, scenarios and requirements."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-component-edit-review.bpmn:166
#. Diagram label
msgid "reject"
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-component-edit-review.bpmn:92
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Render the component the way its reviewer reads it (column \"renderer and diff\"): the BPMN diagram (render:bpmn) with a visual-diff picture; the DMN decision table (smart-base-transform.py dmn2html) with each rule's L1 citation; the data dictionary's term diff (dak-data-dictionary-diff.ts) and the chosen wireframe of each form; personas, scenarios and requirements as a prose diff. Commit to the feature branch so it is staged as STAGING/<slug>/ on the platform's just-the-docs site (for smart-base, a folio-assistant staging re-pin, never the IG's /deploy), and make the before/after preview here, in the producing lane, so it exists when review starts."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-component-edit-review.bpmn:91
#. Diagram label
msgid "Render, stage, before/after [before-after-preview · feature-staging]"
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-component-edit-review.bpmn:143
#. Diagram label
msgid "Reopen upstream, flag derived assets [todo-manager]"
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-component-edit-review.bpmn:165
#. Diagram label
msgid "request-changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-component-edit-review.bpmn:101
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Review forks alongside, it never blocks (owner, 2026-10-14). One branch hands the component on at once; the other asks for review. The process instance ends only when both have ended, so not waiting is not skipping."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-component-edit-review.bpmn:119
#. Diagram label
msgid "Review the staged component [content-review]"
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-component-edit-review.bpmn:81
#. Diagram label
msgid "Run the component's checker [content-validate · content-test]"
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-component-edit-review.bpmn:107
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The calling track continues with this component. Anything derived from it carries adjudication: pending on its wasDerivedFrom edge until the verdict is recorded (smart-guideline-end-to-end, rule 2)."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-component-edit-review.bpmn:82
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The mechanical checks for this component, before anyone is asked (skill l2-component-edit-review, column \"checker\"): BPMN imports in bpmn-js with no warnings and its lanes map to personas (dak-swimlanes.ts); DMN loads, its decisions are reachable (artefact-reachability, audit:reachability) and its test cases run (content-test); the data dictionary's ids are unique and its references and terminology bindings resolve (check-dak-annexes.ts); personas, scenarios and requirements each trace to an L1 recommendation (recommendation-extraction's implementedBy edges). Findings travel with the review request; a failing check does not stop the hand-on, it is a finding the reviewer sees."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-component-edit-review.bpmn:130
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The reviewer's recorded Decision outcome: approve ends the review; request-changes sends the component back to the edit, which re-stages it and asks again; reject means the component is wrong at the root (wrong source, wrong dependency) and reopens the stage that chose it. The calling track has not waited for any of these."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-component-edit-review.bpmn:152
#. Diagram label
msgid "Upstream stage reopened"
msgstr ""

